// Filename:	Spotlight Array PCB.test
// Project:		VSC90,VSC90,VSC80,VSC800
// Author:      Foster & Freeman Ltd - Paul Evans
// Modified:    
//
// Description: Tests the Spotlight Array PCB.
// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

[0] force FAIL by default to avoid IMPORTANT message below.

#1: Enter operator initials and PCB serial number:
a. Enter operator intials.
b. Enter serial number into the box below.
IMPORTANT: Observe ESD precautions for handling ESD sensitive devices.  
//DISPLAY: lamptrayPCB1.jpg
CLICK_OK:

#2: Equipment Setup 1
a. Using TE159 connect the PSU to the VSC90 Controller Test Box(TE209).
b. Connect the PC (via USB) to K5 on the Test box (TE209).
c. Connect the PC (via USB) to the TENMA Programmable PSU.
d. Connect the PC to the LED Test Box with Web Camera (TE086).
//DISPLAY: TE132.jpg
CLICK_OK:


#3: Equipment Setup 2
a. Connect the UUT to the VSC90 Controller Test Box(TE209).
b. Place the UUT inside the LED Test Box with Web Camera (TE086).
c. Set the TENMA Programmable PSU power switch to on.
CLICK_OK:
EXE: OpenWinCam.bat
CONNECT: TENMAPSU
IF_NOT:
GOTO: #3: 

#4: Configure the PSU
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCP1
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCPSET1:500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET1:12.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET1:1.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET2:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET2:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH1:1

#4.1: Power on the test box.
Press the I/O Power button on the VSC90 Controller Test Box(TE209) to turn on.
DELAY: 7000
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned voltage is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.085 0.010 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
IF:
GOTO: #4.2: 
IMPORTANT: This test has failed, check the power button has been pressed, power supply, USB connection and the ftdi chip.		
PASS_FAIL: #4.1
GOTO: #5

#4.2: Connect to the test box
CONNECT: VSC90
IF_NOT: 
GOTO: #4.1:

#5: PCB communication check
COMMAND: VSC90 SPOTSHIFT 1 //. This allows the Spot PCB to be directly plugged into the control PCB 
COMMAND: VSC90 ENUM
READLINE: VSC90 ENUM 
Check the expected result is a match.
Expected result is = SPOT,TEMP,ZOOM,EEPROM,
Returned result is = %ENUM%
[%ENUM% STR_EQ SPOT,TEMP,ZOOM,EEPROM,]// evaluates inside the [] and set true or false flag
SUB: TestPassOrFail // sends the outcome to flag to the subroutine for evaluation

#6: Test the VIOLET LED
COMMAND: VSC90 VIOLET 1023
DELAY: 2500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.280 0.005 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail

#7: Test the BLUE LED
COMMAND: VSC90 BLUE 100
DELAY: 2500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.258 0.005 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail

#8: Test the BLUEGREEN LED
COMMAND: VSC90 BLUEGREEN 100
DELAY: 2500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.277 0.005 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail

#9: Test the CYAN LED
COMMAND: VSC90 CYAN 100
DELAY: 2500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.273 0.005 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail

#10: Test the RED LED
COMMAND: VSC90 RED 100
DELAY: 2500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.227 0.005 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail

#11: Test the GREEN LED
COMMAND: VSC90 GREEN 500
DELAY: 2500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.273 0.005 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail

#12: Test the DEEPRED LED
COMMAND: VSC90 DEEPRED 1023
DELAY: 2500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.226 0.005 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail

#13: Test the AMBER LED
COMMAND: VSC90 AMBER 100
DELAY: 2500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.257 0.005 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail

#13: Test the FARRED LED
COMMAND: VSC90 FARRED 100
DELAY: 2500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.214 0.005 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail

#14: Test the WHITESPOT LED
COMMAND: VSC90 WHITESPOT 100
DELAY: 2500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.259 0.005 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail

#15: Test's Complete
COMMAND: VSC90 off
IF: %FAILED% > 0
GOTO: #Failed:
ELSE: #Passed:


#Failed: a test failed
This PCB has failed to pass all Tests
Check the Log file for more details on the failed test(s).
IMPORTANT: This PCB has failed to pass all Tests
DISPLAY: test_failed.png
CLICK_OK:
GOTO: #QUIT:

#Passed: Test's Complete
a. All tests instructions have been completed and a log file created.
b. Click OK to finish and power OFF.
DISPLAY: AllTestsPassed.png
CLICK_OK:

#QUIT:
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET1:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET1:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0
EXE: CloseWinCam.bat
// End of file
